\includegraphics[width=\columnwidth]{figures/fig_r2_collapse.pdf}
\caption{Per-layer $R^2$ action-probe profiles for three architectures, each comparing trained (solid) and untrained (dashed) checkpoints.
All six VLM-to-VLA cells (TracVLA and NORA, 6/6) exhibit pronounced peak-to-exit collapse ($\Delta R^2 = 0.14$--$0.69$), while their untrained VLM baselines show flat profiles ($\Delta R^2 \leq 0.05$).
In contrast, only 1 of 3 OXE-to-LIBERO cells (OpenVLA Object, $\Delta R^2 = 0.12$) shows collapse; OpenVLA's untrained baseline is an OXE-pretrained VLA that has already undergone exit-layer reorganization.
One-sided sign test confirms the VLM-to-VLA direction across all six cells ($p = 0.016$).}
\label{fig:r2_collapse}
\end{figure}

